      "title": "THE CHAPLAIN'S DIARY",
      "text": "Tuesday. The men will not come to the chapel since the floor began to crack. I told them it was the frost. Tonight I put my ear to the stones and heard something under them knocking, patient, as if it knew that someone would come and open the door. God forgive me, I almost did."
    },
